The '''2021–22''' [[Saudi Pro League]] was the 47th edition of the [[Saudi Pro League|top-tier Saudi football league]], established in [[1974–75 Saudi Categorization League|1974]], and the 14th edition since it was rebranded as the '''Saudi Pro League''' in [[2008–09 Saudi Pro League|2008]], Fixtures for the 2021–22 season were announced on 18 July 2021.<ref>{{cite web |title=إعلان مواعيد مباريات دوري المحترفين للموسم الجديد |url=https://akhbaar24.argaam.com/article/detail/556421 |language=ar }}</ref>

[[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] were the two-time defending champions after winning their 17th title [[2020–21 Saudi Professional League|last season]].<ref>{{cite web |title=فريق الهلال يُحقق لقب دوري الأمير محمد بن سلمان للمحترفين قبل جولة من ختام من المسابقة |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/viewfullstory.php?lang=ar&newsid=2230529 |language=ar }}</ref> [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]], [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]], and [[Al-Tai FC|Al-Tai]] join as the three promoted clubs from the [[2020–21 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|2020–21 MS League]].<ref>{{cite web |title=بعد تأهل الحزم والفيحاء.. الطائي يصعد لدوري كأس الأمير محمد بن سلمان للمحترفين |url=https://sabq.org/JnS4By |language=ar }}</ref> They replace [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]], [[Al-Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]], and [[Al-Wehda Club (Mecca)|Al-Wehda]] who were relegated to the [[2021–22 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|2021–22 MS League]].

On 27 June, [[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] secured their eighteenth league title in the final matchday following a 2–1 home win against [[Al Faisaly FC|Al-Faisaly]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الهلال يُتّوج بلقب دوري المحترفين للمرة الثالثة على التوالي |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/viewstory.php?lang=ar&newsid=2366007}}</ref> It was also the club's third consecutive title and fifth in the last six seasons. [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]] were the first team to be relegated following a 5–2 defeat away to [[Ettifaq FC|Al-Ettifaq]] on 21 May.<ref>{{cite web |title=الاتفاق يتنفس الصعداء ويؤكد هبوط الحزم |url=https://lym.news/a/6397942 |language=ar }}</ref> In the final matchday, both [[Al Faisaly FC|Al-Faisaly]] and [[Al-Ahli Saudi FC|Al-Ahli]] were relegated following a defeat to [[Al Hilal SFC|Al-Hilal]] and a draw with [[Al-Shabab FC (Riyadh)|Al-Shabab]] respectively.

==Overview==
===Sponsorship===
On 8 August 2021, the Saudi Professional League announced that they had signed a sponsorship deal with real estate company [[Roshn]].<ref>{{cite web |title=شركة روشن راعٍ لدوري كأس الأمير محمد بن سلمان للمحترفين |url=https://sabq.org/rzvqHJ}}</ref> On 9 August 2021, the Saudi FF signed a sponsorship deal with Chinese [[Technology company|tech company]] [[Lenovo]] to become the official technology partner of all Saudi football competitions.<ref>{{cite web |title=اتحاد القدم يوقع عقداً مع "لينوفو" لتكون شريكاً تقنياً للاتحاد السعودي والمنتخبات الوطنية |url=https://www.okaz.com.sa/sport/saudi/2078168}}</ref>

===Changes===
On 8 August 2021, [[Ministry of Sports (Saudi Arabia)|Ministry of Sports]] announced that they had increased the capacity limit from 40% to 60% in all stadiums. It was also announced that children under 12 wouldn't be allowed to attend matches and that the attendance would be limited to those who are fully vaccinated.<ref>{{cite web |title=رفع نسبة الحضور الجماهيري إلى 60 في المئة |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/738865}}</ref>

