Sixteen teams will compete in the league&nbsp;– the top thirteen teams from the previous season and the three teams promoted from the [[2019–20 Prince Mohammad bin Salman League|MS League]].

'''Teams who were promoted to the Pro League'''

The first club to be promoted was [[Al-Hazem F.C.|Al-Hazem]], who were promoted following a 4–2 away win against [[Al-Sahel FC|Al-Sahel]] on 20 April 2021. Al-Hazem will play in the top flight of Saudi football after a season's absence.<ref>{{cite web |title=رسمياً: الحزم أول الصاعدين إلى دوري الكبار برقم قياسي جديد|url=https://www.dawriplus.com/news/53304-%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7%D9%8B-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%B2%D9%85-%D8%A3%D9%88%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A5%D9%84%D9%89-%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%83%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D9%82%D9%85-%D9%82%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%8A-%D8%AC%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%AF.html}}</ref> Al-Hazem were crowned champions following a 1–0 away win against [[Hajer FC|Hajer]] on 21 May 2021.<ref>{{cite web |title=رياضي / فريق الحزم بطلاً لدوري الدرجة الأولى .. والفيحاء ثاني الصاعدين |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/2230049}}</ref>

The second club to be promoted was [[Al-Fayha FC|Al-Fayha]], following a 0–0 home draw with [[Al-Tai FC|Al-Tai]] on 20 May 2021.<ref>{{cite web |title=الفيحاء.. عودة سريعة إلى المحترفين |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/730375}}</ref> Al-Fayha will play in the top flight of Saudi football after a season's absence.

The third and final club to be promoted was [[Al-Tai FC|Al-Tai]] who were promoted on the final matchday following a 2–0 away win over [[Arar FC|Arar]].<ref>{{cite web |title=الطائي.. ظهور أول في المحترفين |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/731463}}</ref> Al-Tai will play in the top flight of Saudi football for the first time since the [[2007–08 Saudi Premier League|2007–08 season]].

'''Teams who were relegated to the MS League'''

The first club to be relegated was [[Al-Ain FC (Saudi Arabia)|Al-Ain]], who were relegated after only a year in the top flight following a 2–0 defeat away to [[Al-Nassr FC|Al-Nassr]] on 14 May 2021.<ref>{{cite web |title=رسميا.. العين اول الهابطين من الدوري السعودي للمحترفين |url=https://alwafd.news/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B6%D8%A9/3742665-%D8%B1%D8%B3%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%8A%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%88%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%A8%D8%B7%D9%8A%D9%86-%D9%85%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A-%D9%84%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D8%B1%D9%81%D9%8A%D9%86}}</ref>

In the final matchday, both [[Al-Qadsiah FC|Al-Qadsiah]] and [[Al-Wehda Club (Mecca)|Al-Wehda]] were relegated following a draw with [[Abha Club|Abha]] and a loss against [[Al-Shabab FC (Riyadh)|Al-Shabab]] respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=الوحدة والقادسية يودعان.. وضمك والباطن وأبها ينجون |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/731383}}</ref> Al-Qadsiah were relegated after only a year in the top flight while Al-Wehda were relegated after three years in the top flight.

